{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J3", "U25", "C1", "U31"],
      "pins": ["J3.A7", "J3.B7", "U25.4"],
      "nets": ["USBC_D_N"],
      "observed": "The USB-C D- pins (J3 A7/B7) and U25 pin 4 (I/O2, the second I/O2 pin of the USBLC6-2P6) all sit on the same large net as the ground pins of many parts (J3 A1/B1/A12/B12, U25 pin 2, U26 pin 2, C1 pin 2, Module1 GND pins, etc.). That net is named USBC_D_N. Meanwhile U25 pin 3 (the other I/O2 pin) and U24 pin 6 are on the separate net USBCP_D_N.",
      "expected": "USB-C D- should connect to the USB D- data net (with U25 pins 3 and 4 both on the I/O2 line). It must not be tied to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"203\") (name \"USBC_D_N\") (class \"Default\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"A7\") (pinfunction \"D-\") ...) (node (ref \"U25\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"I/O2\") ...)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"201\") (name \"USBCP_D_N\") ... (node (ref \"U25\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"I/O2\") ...)"}
      ],
      "impact": "USB-C D- is shorted to ground. USB 2.0 data on the USB-C port cannot communicate and the ESD clamp's data line is pulled to ground, so USB-C data (and the USB-C path through U24/U25) would fail.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["D30", "R60", "R59"],
      "pins": ["D30.2", "D30.4", "R60.2", "R59.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(D30-K2)", "ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "D30 is a dual LED with anode A2 (pin 4) on ESTOP_OUT. Its K2 cathode (pin 2) goes through R60 whose second end is also on ESTOP_OUT. The companion channel R59 returns its resistor to GND (net 203). The K2 branch therefore forms a loop from ESTOP_OUT back to ESTOP_OUT and carries no current.",
      "expected": "The ESTOP_OUT indicator channel should be anode on ESTOP_OUT, cathode through R60 to GND, mirroring R59 on the K1 channel.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"67\") (name \"ESTOP_OUT\") ... (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") ...) ... (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ..."},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") ... (node (ref \"R59\") (pin \"2\") ..."},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R60 Net-_D30-K2_ ESTOP_OUT 130"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ESTOP_OUT indicator LED never lights, so the e-stop status indication is lost. The rest of the e-stop chain is unaffected.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is valued \"24k\" in the schematic and SPICE deck. Its library description and MPN (FRC0805J240TSD) describe a 24 Ω part.",
      "expected": "The value should match the part description and MPN (24 Ω), or the description and MPN should be corrected to match a 24 kΩ value.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the part is actually 24 Ω across VOUTP/VOUTN, it would load the output heavily. If it is actually 24 kΩ, the description is wrong. Either way, the bleed or divider behaviour is uncertain.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The most likely deviation is the USB-C D- net (J3 A7/B7 and U25 pin 4) being merged with the ground net, which would short the USB data line to ground. Secondary findings are a shorted LED loop on D30/R60 and a value/description mismatch on R36."
}

